  "semantic_claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The majority holds that a federal prisoner's claim that BOP unlawfully withheld First Step Act time credits and thereby his statutory transfer out of prison to a halfway house or home confinement is cognizable under 28 U.S.C. 2241, resting on Preiser v. Rodriguez: transfer from prison into prerelease custody in the community is treated as materially like release to parole, so the claim attacks the fact or duration of confinement in prison; the Fifth Circuit's Melot 'automatic accelerated release' bright-line rule is rejected."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The holding is narrow: it is confined to claims seeking release from a prison into community-based prerelease custody (halfway house or home confinement), expressly declines to adopt petitioner's general 'distinct and lower level of custody' test, reserves intra-prison security-level transfers, and expressly leaves the 3621(b) judicial-review bar, exhaustion and mootness for remand without deciding them."
    }
  ],
